    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28268.\">Fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1827863221\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28268\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/28268/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28268\">#28268</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An overwhelming proportion of this article talks about CSS, and has nothing to do with either DOM or HTML. As such, I think it would be better to just rebrand this article wholesale as one about CSS whitespace processing. This does strand the \"Whitespace in DOM\" section a bit, but it's short and more like an aside anyway, and we eventually tie back to the \"rendered\" aspect anyway when talking about selection and <code class=\"notranslate\">innerText</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/yarusome/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/yarusome\">@yarusome</a></p>",
